{"id": "EUVD-2026-95080", "enisaUuid": "62a7e99c-87ed-30c1-9990-71340d8ed540", "description": "FFmpeg through 9.0.2 contains a missing host key verification vulnerability in the libssh-based sftp protocol handler that allows network attackers to impersonate SFTP servers. Attackers performing man-in-the-middle, DNS, or ARP spoofing can capture passwords supplied in sftp URLs, serve forged media, or receive uploaded output.", "datePublished": "2026-10-08T15:28:41", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-08T18:00:38", "baseScore": 6.0, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:H/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:L/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/pulls/24384", "https://code.ffmpeg.org/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/commit/2b822b7fb6ed195546bc9fd9bdb794e98222bdce", "https://github.com/FFmpeg/FFmpeg/blob/n9.0.2/libavformat/libssh.c#L60-L110", "https://ffmpeg.org/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ffmpeg-through-9.0.2-missing-ssh-host-key-verification-in-sftp-protocol"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-107675", "GHSA-vv62-hhh4-f6vv"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "6371683e-4101-3780-bad8-ef1422146c66", "product": {"name": "FFmpeg", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22649.0.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "9b52a477-a7a6-3b08-872d-0a561690bebf", "vendor": {"name": "FFMPEG"}}], "isExploited": false}